@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP core / cross-cutting. Core presentation/application/files or shared authority/recovery invariant remains applicable.
title Proposed current authority and revocation boundary
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam shadowing false

actor Caller
participant "Resource-owning handler" as H
participant "Identity / authority contract" as I
database "Current account / session / grant state" as DB
Caller -> H : intended resource / action / expected version
H -> I : resolve current attributable context
I -> DB : current eligibility / policy / scoped state
DB --> I : actual versioned context
I --> H : bounded authority decision / denial
H -> H : current resource lifecycle and operation invariant
note over H,DB
 Concrete synchronization must cover grant/account-change races.
 A positive check is not an indefinitely reusable capability.
end note
alt permitted
 H -> H : admit exact owned operation
 H --> Caller : permitted attributable result
else denied / unresolved authority
 H --> Caller : safe denial; no unauthorized mutation/disclosure
end
note over I,DB
 Revocation completion defines when subsequent decisions see new state.
 Already emitted bytes / admitted external effects are not recalled.
end note
@enduml
